---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SocialIcons from '../components/SocialIcons.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Me"
  description="Background, career journey, security competencies, and academic research of Mohammad Ishfaque Jahan Rafee."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1 class="page-title">About Me</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">
      Hi, I'm <strong>{SITE.title}</strong> — a <strong>{SITE.role}</strong> based in {SITE.location}. Most people know me as <strong>{SITE.shortName}</strong> or online as <a href={SITE.socials.twitter} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{SITE.socials.twitterHandle}</a>.
    </p>
  </header>

  <article class="prose">
    <p>
      I specialize in <strong>Cloud Security Architecture (AWS &amp; OCI)</strong>, <strong>Infrastructure Defense</strong>, <strong>Digital Forensics &amp; Incident Response (DFIR)</strong>, and <strong>Security Automation</strong>. My engineering philosophy centers on building pragmatic, robust defenses that empower development and operations rather than slowing them down.
    </p>

    <h2>My Journey</h2>
    <p>
      My passion for engineering and mathematics began in Bangladesh, which led me to study Electrical and Electronic Engineering at the country's premier institution, the <strong>Bangladesh University of Engineering and Technology (BUET)</strong>.
    </p>

    <h3>Technical Pre-Sales &amp; Enterprise Telecom</h3>
    <p>
      Following graduation, I spent four formative years in telecommunications and enterprise solutions:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Huawei Technologies — Solutions Engineer</strong>: Communicated across the entire organizational spectrum. I worked directly with seasoned technical teams on granular technical details while articulating business impact, ROI, and security postures to C-suite/CXO executives.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>ZTE Corporation — Technical Account Manager / Pre-Sales</strong>: Led technical consulting and account management for large-scale telecommunications and government infrastructure projects, including a multi-vendor project valued near <strong>USD $200M</strong>. Managing such complex engagements honed my ability to anticipate risks, coordinate cross-functional teams, and ensure robust operational governance.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Graduate Studies &amp; Systems Security</h3>
    <p>
      Driven by an enduring enthusiasm for cloud systems, networks, and cybersecurity, I moved to Canada to pursue my graduate degree at <strong>Concordia University</strong> in Montreal. I earned my <strong>Master of Engineering (MEng) in Information Systems Security</strong>, while also working as a Graduate Research Assistant investigating computer vision, projective geometry, and distributed systems.
    </p>

    <h3>Security Engineering at CMiC</h3>
    <p>
      Today, I work as a <strong>Security Engineer at CMiC</strong>, where I safeguard enterprise ERP cloud environments across <strong>Amazon Web Services (AWS)</strong> and <strong>Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI)</strong>:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Implementing continuous risk management, threat modeling, and proactive security guardrails.</li>
      <li>Designing and implementing automated security auditing and compliance checks using <strong>Python</strong> and <strong>Go</strong>.</li>
      <li>Analyzing SIEM telemetry, network flow logs, and infrastructure configurations to detect anomalies and strengthen defense-in-depth posture.</li>
      <li>Championing <strong>Infrastructure as Code (IaC)</strong> with Terraform to ensure our cloud environments remain reproducible, auditable, and secure by default.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Systems Engineering &amp; Current Endeavors: Unhurried</h3>
    <p>
      Beyond enterprise cloud security, I am actively architecting <a href="https://github.com/Unhurried-Careers" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Unhurried</strong></a> — a distributed, cloud-native platform on Google Cloud (built with Go microservices, Cloud Run, API Gateway, Firestore, and React) engineered to replace AI application spam with deliberate, curated career research and high-intent candidate outreach.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Technical Toolkit &amp; Competencies</h2>
    <div class="skills-grid not-prose">
      <div class="card skill-card">
        <h3>Cloud &amp; Defense</h3>
        <p>Amazon Web Services (AWS), Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI), Cloud Security Posture Management (CSPM), IAM, Zero-Trust Architecture, Linux/Unix, Docker.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card skill-card">
        <h3>DFIR &amp; Threat Analysis</h3>
        <p>Digital Forensics &amp; Incident Response, Memory Forensics (Volatility 2 &amp; 3), SIEM Log Ingestion, Network Traffic Inspection, Vulnerability Assessment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card skill-card">
        <h3>Automation &amp; Scripting</h3>
        <p>Python, Go, Bash, REST APIs, automated security auditing and remediation scripts, CI/CD pipeline verification.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card skill-card">
        <h3>IaC &amp; Engineering</h3>
        <p>Terraform, CloudFormation, GitOps workflows, Algorithmic problem solving in Go, Python, Java, C++ (300+ LeetCode solved).</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr />

    <h2>Academic Publications &amp; Research</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Self-localization of a mobile robot using monocular vision of a chessboard pattern</strong><br />
        <em>IEEE Conference Publication</em><br />
        <em>Co-authors: Parvez Ahmmed, Zabir Ahmed, Sajid Muhaimin Choudhury, Mohammad Rafee</em><br />
        Focus: Mobile robotics, computer vision, projective geometry, and autonomous indoor localization.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Modeling and simulation of a Microcontroller based power factor correction converter</strong><br />
        <em>IEEE Conference Publication</em><br />
        <em>Co-authors: Parvez Ahmmed, Shammya Shananda Saha, S M Nahian Al Sunny, Mohammad Rafee</em><br />
        Focus: Power electronics, microcontroller control loops, and efficiency optimization.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <hr />

    <h2>Beyond the Terminal</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Distance Running</strong>: An avid runner training for marathons and half-marathons, frequently participating in local road races across Alberta and Canada.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Urban Planning &amp; Zoning Advocacy</strong>: Passionate about sustainable urbanism, walkable communities, and housing accessibility — actively engaging with local municipal discussions and civic initiatives in Edmonton.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Security Challenges &amp; Hacking</strong>: Sharpening forensic and offensive defense skills through <strong>Hack The Box</strong> Sherlocks and CTFs.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <h2>Let's Connect</h2>
    <p>
      I am always keen to exchange ideas with fellow security practitioners, cloud architects, developers, and runners.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>LinkedIn</strong>: <a href={SITE.socials.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">linkedin.com/in/rafee-sec</a></li>
      <li><strong>GitHub</strong>: <a href={SITE.socials.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/rafee</a></li>
      <li><strong>X / Twitter</strong>: <a href={SITE.socials.twitter} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{SITE.socials.twitterHandle}</a></li>
      <li><strong>Email</strong>: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></li>
    </ul>

    <div class="not-prose" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
      <SocialIcons />
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .skills-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .skills-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .skill-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .skill-card p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
</style>
